Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:09:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/16] website: no console email on a deployed site (codes and
 addresses reached the logs; students were told a code was sent)

Without a working provider (EMAIL_PROVIDER unset, or smtp without EMAIL_SMTP_HOST) email() fell back to the console
sender, which on every non-production deployment printed `to=<student email> subject="<6-digit code> is your Eduwit
verification code"` to the hosting logs (raw console.info, past the PII scrubber) and reported success. The form
then said "we sent a code" that never arrived, admin second-factor codes went to the same log, and /api/health
called email fine on preview. The live site runs APP_ENV=preview today.

- console sender: on production and preview it logs `email.not_configured` and throws, so the gate answers
  send_failed ("We couldn't send the code just now"), the admin sees "We couldn't send the code" and outbox emails
  retry instead of being marked done; on a developer machine it prints as before.
- emailProvider(): the provider that actually sends; /api/health detail reports it (chosen vs effective) and flags
  console on any deployed site; the Turnstile check also says whether the site key is set.

